# ─── Obsidian ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Volatile UI state: rewritten every time a pane moves, so it would add
# noise to every commit. appearance.json, app.json and core-plugins.json
# are deliberately NOT ignored — those keep the vault reproducible.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache
.trash/

# ─── Claude Code ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Machine-local settings plus the temp files written during saves.
.claude/

# ─── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ─── Compiled C artifacts from lab starters ──────────────────────────
*.o
*.out
*.exe
a.out
# extensionless ELF binary built by the PROG 101 Week 0 starter
0. Freshman/Fall/1. PROG 101 - Programming I: Structured Programming in C/PROG101 Week0/lab/starter/hello

# ─── OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Submissions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each course under here gets its own git repo with its own remote
# (e.g. CS 101 -> ZerosAndOnesGlover/cs101). Tracking them from the
# vault repo would leave stray gitlinks pointing at commits this repo
# does not contain. Commit and push each course from inside its own
# directory instead.
/5. Academic Registry/4. Submissions/
